# Agent Prompt System — intent compiler preflight

For **substantial** tasks, compile an IntentContract before large edits. Prefer the `aps-router` Skill. Soft enforcement (advisory) unless Gate C hooks are later earned.

## APS brief (first user-visible paragraph)

```text
Selected workflows: <id-1>, <id-2?>
```

Then the rendered `APS INTENT CONTRACT` (see `agent-prompt-system/templates/cursor-instruction.md`).

## Preflight checklist

1. Preserve user intent; increase precision, never ambition.
2. Read `agent-prompt-system/core/request-router.md` + `manifest.json` → ≤3 workflows / `taskType`.
3. Discover project evidence; resolve `project-context/` pointers → `project-knowledge/` (or `rpb_read_project_doc`).
4. Ask only if `core/clarification-gate.md` three conditions hold.
5. Emit eight-field IntentContract; never promote model inference into requirements.
6. Hand off — Cursor agent executes under selected workflows; APS does not execute.
7. End with evidence labels: **Verified** / **Partially verified** / **Not verified** / **Blocked** / **Assumed**.

## Bypass

Simple explanations, locate-a-file, isolated typos, one-line fixes → no full compile.

## Precedence (process, not a verified Cursor global order)

User instruction → safety/security → product boundaries (via north-star / PRODUCT canon) → this router → selected workflows → discovered project evidence.

## Not this system

Runtime product prompts under `src/features/**/prompts/` and Next.js API routes are separate from APS.

